      "writtenOn": "2024-01-23T23:06:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This `filter_map()` pattern could potentially be replaced by a helper in libavb_rs:\n\n```\nlet mut iter \u003d filter_descriptors::\u003cPropertyDescriptor\u003e(descriptors);\n```\n\nthe catch is that the implementation of such a helper was surprisingly complicated just for a 4-line replacement (https://r.android.com/2925251). I\u0027m still on the fence whether it\u0027s worth it or not.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 148,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 151,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "36bac726f6f77a15b42525420ece4d10e721f65a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "19c679cd_ee1888b6",
        "filename": "pvmfw/avb/src/verify.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 151,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-29T09:26:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t feel it\u0027s really worth the effort. The implementation seems to be pretty complex to \"simplify\" just four lines of code here. I think we can just use the `filter_map` here.",
      "parentUuid": "2166c85c_381e2c21",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 148,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 151,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "36bac726f6f77a15b42525420ece4d10e721f65a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "349cf484_9233e295",
        "filename": "pvmfw/avb/src/verify.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 274,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-29T09:26:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we avoid the copy of the digest here? As this code runs in a bare-metal environment with limited resources. We would like to avoid any unnecessary copys.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 274,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 274,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "36bac726f6f77a15b42525420ece4d10e721f65a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d20af477_8bafcfcd",
        "filename": "pvmfw/avb/src/verify.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 274,
      "author": {
        "id": 1078119
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-29T20:00:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately I don\u0027t think it\u0027s possible with the current lifetime definitions, because the verification data borrows `ops` (necessary to borrow the underlying preloaded partition data owned by `ops`).\n\nSo the caller would have to pass in `ops` themselves so the lifetime could outlive the function, but `ops` is an internal implementation detail here so we don\u0027t want that.\n\nFWIW, as I understand it the current code is also copying the digest array, so this doesn\u0027t add any additional memory overhead, it just makes it more explicit via the `copy_digest` function rather than relying on array\u0027s built-in `Copy` trait.\n\nNow that I\u0027m a little more familiar with lifetimes, I *think* it may be possible to be a little more precise with the `Ops` trait lifetimes in libavb_rs such that we can split the preloaded data lifetime apart from the `Ops` object itself, which should allow the verification result to borrow only the preloadeded data (which outlives this function) rather than `ops` (which does not). But this may be a more significant refactor, and since this CL does the same amount of copying as the current implementation, I think it might be best left to a future CL. WDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "349cf484_9233e295",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 274,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 274,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "36bac726f6f77a15b42525420ece4d10e721f65a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "30138f28_1aa81250",
        "filename": "pvmfw/avb/src/verify.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 274,
      "author": {
        "id": 1078119
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-01T01:36:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For reference, I think I got it working to split the `Ops` lifetime apart from the preloaded data lifetime: https://r.android.com/2942445.\n\nIt\u0027s more involved than I had hoped and I still need to test it out with pvmfw to make sure it works in practice, but I *think* this will solve a lot of the lifetime awkwardness by separating the `Ops` lifetime from the returned `SlotVerifyData` lifetime.",
      "parentUuid": "d20af477_8bafcfcd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 274,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 274,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "36bac726f6f77a15b42525420ece4d10e721f65a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "82f569d5_62cbad83",
        "filename": "pvmfw/avb/src/verify.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 274,
      "author": {
        "id": 1078119
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-02T20:32:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, spent a bit more time playing around with it, and I think keeping the copy here is the best solution.\n\nThe reason is that the digests are part of the vbmeta blob which is loaded into heap memory by libavb and now owned by `kernel_verify_result`. So if we want to just return a reference here rather than an array copy, we also have to take ownership of the underlying data so it doesn\u0027t go out of scope, which essentially means hanging onto the entire `kernel_verify_result` ourselves - much larger than just making a copy of the digest.\n\nSplitting lifetimes in the above CL does still make using `Ops` a little simpler though, for example in line 283 below we would no longer need to create a new `Ops` object for the second verification since `kernel_verify_result` wouldn\u0027t borrow the first `ops` anymore.",
      "parentUuid": "30138f28_1aa81250",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 274,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 274,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "36bac726f6f77a15b42525420ece4d10e721f65a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
